1
00:02:09,389 --> 00:02:26,550
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:03:05,330 --> 00:03:07,550
Welcome, Osman Bey.

3
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:18,750
Tell me.

4
00:03:22,050 --> 00:03:22,900
Beys!

5
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:27,680
Alps!

6
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:31,490
Why would someone going to
a conquest be sad?

7
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:34,610
It's because we are ashamed, my bey.

8
00:03:36,190 --> 00:03:38,050
We didn't trust you.

9
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:40,420
We believed the plot against Turgut Bey.

10
00:03:40,670 --> 00:03:42,050
We regret it.

11
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:46,240
Which regret is this?

12
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:49,120
Which hesitation is this?

13
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:56,750
If you don't take lessons from
the past...

14
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,760
how will you look into the future?

15
00:04:04,210 --> 00:04:06,430
Our target is Yenişehir.

16
00:04:07,410 --> 00:04:08,640
İznik!

17
00:04:09,230 --> 00:04:11,300
And Bursa!

18
00:04:12,850 --> 00:04:13,980
But...

19
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:20,060
with those who don't trust the leader,
you can't reach anywhere.

20
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:26,780
With those who don't listen to the bey,
you can't conquer anything.

21
00:04:28,020 --> 00:04:33,300
If anyone doubts the gray wolf again,
may our swords turn red with our blood!

22
00:04:33,790 --> 00:04:34,720
This is the last.

23
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:37,310
We follow your decisions, Osman Bey.

24
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:38,940
Think me as your arrow.

25
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:40,940
I go wherever you
release me to.

26
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:43,220
Say strike and we'll strike.

27
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,450
Barkın's end is a lesson to us, my bey.

28
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:52,180
Turgut Bey, give us your blessing.

29
00:04:52,850 --> 00:04:54,180
It's yours.

30
00:04:54,770 --> 00:04:56,580
Let's not repeat it.

31
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:03,200
Don't throw a wolf of yours to
the jackals because of slander.

32
00:05:05,390 --> 00:05:11,020
One calamity is better than
a thousand pieces of advice.

33
00:05:12,530 --> 00:05:14,460
But forgiving won't do.

34
00:05:15,810 --> 00:05:18,110
Those who have the heart
should follow us...

35
00:05:19,090 --> 00:05:21,040
if you don't have the heart...

36
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:24,180
stay back.

37
00:05:48,030 --> 00:05:50,260
I've listened to many tales on
these lands.

38
00:05:50,670 --> 00:05:59,500
Many of them were telling how Osman
turned into a great bey from a young man.

39
00:05:59,970 --> 00:06:04,460
And a few of them were telling about
the heroism of the lords.

40
00:06:06,610 --> 00:06:09,010
But every tale has an end.

41
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:12,530
And Osman's ends here.

42
00:06:13,980 --> 00:06:15,790
If Osman ends...

43
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:18,270
so will the Turks.

44
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:21,550
Osman chose here as a quarter,
Commander Romanos.

45
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:25,280
It's wide and open.
Close to assaults.

46
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:28,590
What kind of an attack
will bring this end?

47
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:31,490
Do you know what he told me?

48
00:06:35,490 --> 00:06:39,580
-If you want to ambush a wolf...
-You must be smarter.

49
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:44,110
I'm smarter than him.

50
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:49,030
Right.

51
00:06:49,550 --> 00:06:51,020
This place is well-protected.

52
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:57,460
But this is why he won't expect
an ambush here.

53
00:07:02,530 --> 00:07:05,360
Great soldiers of the Rome!

54
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:09,440
Osman who spilled your blood...

55
00:07:11,490 --> 00:07:13,490
who took your lands...

56
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:17,620
who stole your property...

57
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:21,260
will be here soon!

58
00:07:25,330 --> 00:07:27,020
Is his grave ready?

59
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:29,020
It is!

60
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:34,740
I prepared a beautiful trap for them.

61
00:07:49,930 --> 00:07:52,710
Yenişehir

62
00:07:59,090 --> 00:08:01,040
Come on, brothers!

63
00:08:01,090 --> 00:08:02,850
It's the day of jihad!

64
00:08:03,070 --> 00:08:05,340
-Allah is eternal!
-Allah is righteous!

65
00:08:05,410 --> 00:08:07,870
We'll hang on until Osman Bey
comes, inshallah!

66
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:08,490
Are the warriors training in
İnegöl ready, Turgut Bey?

67
00:09:08,490 --> 00:09:10,350
Mashallah to all of them.

68
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:12,850
To not get spotted...

69
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:15,440
they are divided in Yılanlık.

70
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:16,740
Thank you.

71
00:09:17,710 --> 00:09:18,860
-Boran.
-My bey.

72
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:20,290
Close all the roads.

73
00:09:20,830 --> 00:09:23,300
No caravan will go to Yenişehir.

74
00:09:23,390 --> 00:09:24,850
As my bey orders.

75
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:35,170
Konur, alps will position here.

76
00:09:36,290 --> 00:09:38,140
Set the tent here.

77
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:39,300
As you order, my bey.

78
00:09:40,290 --> 00:09:41,300
Come on!

79
00:09:50,430 --> 00:09:52,180
Who is this brother?

80
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,680
See him as you see me, my bey.

81
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:58,060
It's Koygan.

82
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:02,580
I came with the envoy
but didn't return.

83
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:04,580
I follow the righteous path, my bey.

84
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:06,880
I wish to be under your command.

85
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:08,590
Thank you.

86
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:12,130
Our doors are open to anyone
who's heart is beating with us.

87
00:10:12,250 --> 00:10:13,860
-Welcome.
-Thank you, my bey.

88
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:20,480
Let's check around.

89
00:10:24,050 --> 00:10:26,420
Let's be sure of where we stand.

90
00:10:26,770 --> 00:10:28,380
With the name of Allah.

91
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,780
Come on.

92
00:10:45,150 --> 00:10:46,660
Hold there, old men!

93
00:10:49,180 --> 00:10:49,950
Where?

94
00:10:50,290 --> 00:10:54,450
I'll take your heathen head with
my sword!

95
00:10:56,450 --> 00:10:58,220
You are surrounded.
Lower your swords.

96
00:11:00,080 --> 00:11:01,140
Kumral.

97
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:04,480
Being a martyr is sweet but...

98
00:11:04,770 --> 00:11:07,580
dying away from home
hurts me.

99
00:11:08,350 --> 00:11:09,970
Hold there, Master Davud.

100
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:15,520
Maybe these lands will turn into
home before we die!

101
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:17,520
Inshallah.

102
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:19,820
Inshallah!

103
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:23,340
It's harmful to dream this much
at this age, old men.

104
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:25,900
You all will die.

105
00:11:26,030 --> 00:11:27,540
And Rome will always be here.

106
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:30,720
Demon. You will die first.

107
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:36,030
-Then, Allah is eternal!
-Allah is righteous!

108
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:14,630
My God, protect them!

109
00:12:36,190 --> 00:12:37,260
Alps!

110
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:40,350
Shield wall!

111
00:12:46,590 --> 00:12:47,650
Hang on!

112
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:56,700
Hang on, alps!

113
00:13:00,270 --> 00:13:01,500
Hang on!

114
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:26,910
Look at them!

115
00:13:36,990 --> 00:13:38,430
Romanos!

116
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:41,790
Come here!
Come here!

117
00:13:48,070 --> 00:13:52,400
Alps! Attack!

118
00:14:38,470 --> 00:14:39,580
Wait.

119
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:43,650
Who are you?
Where are you from?

120
00:14:57,940 --> 00:14:59,550
We are from İznik.

121
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:02,930
We came to support you in
your war against the Turks.

122
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:13,350
We brought provisions
for the people...

123
00:15:14,590 --> 00:15:16,750
and medicine for the physicians.

124
00:15:17,910 --> 00:15:19,440
I thought you were informed.

125
00:15:19,790 --> 00:15:22,040
We sent the news before
moving out.

126
00:15:22,180 --> 00:15:24,680
Welcome. We'll still search
as a caution.

127
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:27,700
Soldiers! We'll search the carts.

128
00:15:34,270 --> 00:15:36,270
Get down.
We'll search.

129
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:37,760
We brought provisions.

130
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:40,700
The people of İznik sent it for
the people of Yenişehir.

131
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:50,750
We took a long way here.
We are tired.

132
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:54,920
But if you want so,
let's get down.

133
00:16:04,050 --> 00:16:04,930
Soldier!

134
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,710
Our guests from İznik?

135
00:16:08,710 --> 00:16:09,580
Yes, sir.

136
00:16:10,580 --> 00:16:12,110
You fools!

137
00:16:12,110 --> 00:16:14,110
Is this how you treat people
helping you?

138
00:16:14,850 --> 00:16:16,640
Leave the carts and
get inside.

139
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:18,050
Yes, commander.

140
00:16:19,950 --> 00:16:22,260
Welcome. Please.

141
00:16:22,260 --> 00:16:23,200
Let them pass.

142
00:16:25,650 --> 00:16:27,170
We are grateful, commander.

143
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:45,170
You'll find Kumral Abdal.

144
00:17:07,618 --> 00:17:08,630
Boran.

145
00:17:22,470 --> 00:17:25,050
Allahu Akbar!

146
00:17:34,050 --> 00:17:35,400
Romanos!

147
00:18:26,410 --> 00:18:31,430
Will we be captives
in the hands of the infidels?

148
00:18:31,630 --> 00:18:34,310
Like Prophet Joseph.

149
00:18:34,310 --> 00:18:38,210
If our destiny is a dungeon,
we appreciate it too.

150
00:18:39,270 --> 00:18:47,210
But this heart wants to die in a battle
for Allah, not in a dungeon.

151
00:18:47,870 --> 00:18:50,350
The infidel's chain
isn't enough for us.

152
00:18:51,530 --> 00:18:54,850
Then, Allah is eternal!

153
00:18:54,850 --> 00:18:56,850
Allah is righteous!

154
00:19:09,340 --> 00:19:15,720
If you try to run again,
I won't be kind.

155
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:19,460
Take them.

156
00:19:30,830 --> 00:19:32,380
To the horses!

157
00:19:56,340 --> 00:19:58,980
If you fight with a wolf,
you'll fight to the death.

158
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:01,610
Where are you running to?

159
00:20:02,930 --> 00:20:05,020
It's enough of you Turks!

160
00:20:12,350 --> 00:20:13,130
Come.

161
00:20:52,170 --> 00:20:53,820
We lost our way.

162
00:20:55,950 --> 00:20:59,010
But we die on the right way.

163
00:21:03,190 --> 00:21:05,230
There is--

164
00:21:08,410 --> 00:21:09,650
You fought to the death.

165
00:21:11,610 --> 00:21:12,750
Soldiers, come on!

166
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:42,140
We have many martyrs, my bey.

167
00:22:44,950 --> 00:22:45,710
Boran.

168
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:57,480
They knew the way of jihad.

169
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:01,160
This way leads to martyrdom.

170
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:08,740
But it's haram to breathe for those
who take our breath.

171
00:23:30,070 --> 00:23:31,240
Musa Bey.

172
00:23:33,290 --> 00:23:35,970
You walked to martyrdom too.

173
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:43,180
Alps.

174
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:47,830
We'll take Yenişehir.

175
00:23:48,980 --> 00:23:53,870
The names of those who've fallen for
it will be remembered in that city.

176
00:24:01,300 --> 00:24:03,350
Let's do our final duty.

177
00:24:13,300 --> 00:24:16,760
Open the gate!
Commander Romanos is coming!

178
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:24,270
I hope it's good.

179
00:24:24,910 --> 00:24:27,820
Be cautious.

180
00:24:46,540 --> 00:24:49,190
Close the gates!
I don't want any holes!

181
00:24:49,190 --> 00:24:51,430
Increase the guards!
Turks are coming!

182
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:53,840
This will be their grave!

183
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:54,870
Come with me!

184
00:24:58,540 --> 00:25:01,040
Romanos got away from
Osman Bey.

185
00:25:01,780 --> 00:25:03,830
How did he survive
all the traps?

186
00:25:03,830 --> 00:25:05,440
It would be good to kill him.

187
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:07,760
It's getting complicated.

188
00:25:07,760 --> 00:25:10,980
After Aygül comes, we'll
find out what's happening.

189
00:25:15,790 --> 00:25:18,580
-It's not good.
-What's happening?

190
00:25:18,580 --> 00:25:19,830
Where is the smith?

191
00:25:21,910 --> 00:25:28,870
Akça Dervish, Kumral Abdal, the Smith;
they are all caught.

192
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:34,560
Romanos' soldiers got them.

193
00:25:35,390 --> 00:25:37,030
They took them to
the dungeon.

194
00:25:37,030 --> 00:25:38,520
What will we do now?

195
00:25:48,180 --> 00:25:49,260
Now.

196
00:25:52,310 --> 00:25:55,280
What we'll do is very simple.

197
00:25:58,620 --> 00:26:00,830
You'll tell me what
you were doing.

198
00:26:08,430 --> 00:26:11,720
We won't tell anything.

199
00:26:13,630 --> 00:26:18,790
I'm asking again. Your Osman Bey.
Why did he send you?

200
00:26:30,260 --> 00:26:33,260
Alright. You won't speak.

201
00:26:35,600 --> 00:26:40,030
Don't speak. I'll figure it out
anyway.

202
00:26:44,440 --> 00:26:48,060
Our warriors have fallen
for the conquest.

203
00:26:48,640 --> 00:26:51,550
They've fallen, fighting chest to
chest against the heathens.

204
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:55,310
Musa Bey and his alps.

205
00:26:56,750 --> 00:26:58,940
They'll always be in our hearts.

206
00:26:59,350 --> 00:27:02,460
Romanos has the numbers, Osman Bey.

207
00:27:04,510 --> 00:27:08,880
They could've let them pass.
But the lions fought.

208
00:27:09,310 --> 00:27:11,660
May they rest in heaven.

209
00:27:11,660 --> 00:27:13,660
They burned our hearts.

210
00:27:14,430 --> 00:27:16,620
We'll burn them with that fire.

211
00:27:17,880 --> 00:27:21,700
Now, we won't stop until taking
Yenişehir.

212
00:27:21,700 --> 00:27:26,580
We won't sheathe our weapons until
raising Islam's banner there.

213
00:27:30,420 --> 00:27:34,190
My bey, as you ordered,
the women sneaked into Yenişehir.

214
00:27:36,520 --> 00:27:40,200
Firstly, we'll speak.
If they don't hear...

215
00:27:40,500 --> 00:27:43,420
they'll hear the sounds
of our weapons.

216
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:52,000
Alps, we are going to our future city
from the hill of martyrs.

217
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:53,520
Come on.

218
00:28:08,830 --> 00:28:12,180
Romanos is in the castle.
Heknows that Kumral Abdal snuck in.

219
00:28:12,180 --> 00:28:14,180
We'll be more cautious now.

220
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:18,320
We have to save them before
our mission then.

221
00:28:29,580 --> 00:28:31,420
Mashallah, Cerkutay.

222
00:28:34,300 --> 00:28:39,720
I'm telling you. Mother Selcan gave her
honey years ago and it worked now!

223
00:28:44,720 --> 00:28:48,180
But I didn't do the job.
Kumral Abdal did.

224
00:28:48,180 --> 00:28:50,500
He left this to Priest Hristo.

225
00:28:51,440 --> 00:28:52,500
Good.

226
00:28:54,430 --> 00:28:57,340
We'll save him with the map
he found.

227
00:28:58,920 --> 00:29:00,380
The dungeon is here.

228
00:29:00,830 --> 00:29:04,790
Firstly, to enter the dungeon,
we must learn the soldier count.

229
00:29:04,790 --> 00:29:07,740
Let's divide labor.
Some of us will search for them.

230
00:29:07,740 --> 00:29:09,840
The rest will take positions.

231
00:29:09,840 --> 00:29:13,920
Cerkutay, check the dungeon
and the corridors.

232
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:16,270
We should know how many
soldiers are there.

233
00:29:17,820 --> 00:29:19,950
Aygül, talk to the sisters.

234
00:29:19,950 --> 00:29:23,960
They should blend into the people.
No one should suspect anything.

235
00:29:23,960 --> 00:29:28,070
Don't worry, they'll walk on the snow
but leave no trace.

236
00:29:29,340 --> 00:29:30,550
Come on, Cerkutay.

237
00:30:00,190 --> 00:30:02,030
Is this how you'll carry
that shield?

238
00:30:08,360 --> 00:30:11,670
Is this how you'll protect the lands
against Turkish arrows?

239
00:30:13,150 --> 00:30:15,360
I'm asking you?

240
00:30:15,800 --> 00:30:19,980
This is how you hold a shield!

241
00:30:20,290 --> 00:30:22,890
-Go and hang him!
-No, sir!

242
00:30:23,110 --> 00:30:25,710
I want to die fighting.
Not for nothing.

243
00:30:25,740 --> 00:30:30,320
Then carry the shield worthy of
a Roman soldier!

244
00:30:33,660 --> 00:30:36,260
Because if you don't...

245
00:30:36,870 --> 00:30:39,620
we all will die today.

246
00:30:39,620 --> 00:30:41,620
We all will die!

247
00:30:42,090 --> 00:30:46,850
Turks killed everyone in İnegöl and
Bilecik...

248
00:30:47,050 --> 00:30:50,310
who refused to be slaves.

249
00:30:50,950 --> 00:30:57,390
Women, priests, children...

250
00:30:59,630 --> 00:31:02,560
they stole properties...

251
00:31:02,770 --> 00:31:07,020
they burned churches,
they destroyed stores!

252
00:31:10,430 --> 00:31:12,650
The dead are gone...

253
00:31:14,300 --> 00:31:16,800
the remaining are slaves.

254
00:31:19,170 --> 00:31:22,270
But I won't allow this.

255
00:31:23,750 --> 00:31:26,630
Your emperor is with you!

256
00:31:28,310 --> 00:31:34,270
He sent me to protect you.

257
00:31:34,670 --> 00:31:37,370
Don't be afraid of the Turks!

258
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:41,290
Commander Romanos!

259
00:31:41,650 --> 00:31:44,250
Commander Romanos!

260
00:31:46,340 --> 00:31:49,390
Osman Bey wishes to speak to you, sir.

261
00:32:01,870 --> 00:32:04,750
He'll want me to surrender the city.

262
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:09,280
-What will we do?
-Spread my words here.

263
00:32:09,660 --> 00:32:12,310
They should afraid of the Turks
like monsters.

264
00:32:12,490 --> 00:32:14,830
Invite them to resistance.

265
00:32:18,190 --> 00:32:23,110
I need to recruit everyone now.

266
00:32:23,340 --> 00:32:26,390
-I'll do what it takes.
-So will I.

267
00:32:27,460 --> 00:32:29,960
I'll talk to Osman.

268
00:33:26,290 --> 00:33:29,420
When you were holding İnegöl
with Nikola...

269
00:33:30,670 --> 00:33:33,850
I sent you Darius' head.

270
00:33:36,960 --> 00:33:40,880
I took Nikola's head in front
of your eyes.

271
00:33:43,190 --> 00:33:49,310
And now, the traitor Barkın's head.

272
00:33:53,640 --> 00:33:55,960
See his fate.

273
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:59,900
And know who's next.

274
00:34:04,820 --> 00:34:08,080
So, my head it at the tip
of your sword, huh?

275
00:34:10,600 --> 00:34:12,560
It's not important.

276
00:34:13,219 --> 00:34:16,460
What's important is the security
of the people of Yenişehir.

277
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:22,920
Give me Yenişehir in peace.

278
00:34:24,889 --> 00:34:29,550
Neither your soldiers nor the civilians
should get hurt.

279
00:34:30,790 --> 00:34:38,360
The elders of the city, the commanders...
I can't decide on that alone.

280
00:34:38,659 --> 00:34:42,940
And also, how can I trust you?

281
00:34:43,270 --> 00:34:47,350
When did we ever dishonor
our word?

282
00:34:48,060 --> 00:34:52,310
Give me Yenişehir and no one
will get hurt.

283
00:35:07,740 --> 00:35:09,300
Alright.

284
00:35:10,600 --> 00:35:12,660
Give me some time.

285
00:35:13,190 --> 00:35:15,760
I'll try to convince them.

286
00:35:18,180 --> 00:35:20,860
I give you time until tomorrow.

287
00:35:21,520 --> 00:35:24,090
Don't hold anything back.

288
00:35:24,350 --> 00:35:28,850
But when the words are over...

289
00:35:29,180 --> 00:35:31,880
the swords will speak.

290
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:41,510
Come on!

291
00:35:52,230 --> 00:35:55,310
Yenişehir

292
00:35:55,390 --> 00:35:57,480
They are protecting the dungeon well.

293
00:35:57,730 --> 00:36:02,240
There are two corridors to there and
both are filled with soldiers.

294
00:36:04,890 --> 00:36:08,270
Did you see Kumral Abdal and
Master Davud?

295
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:11,050
They don't let anyone in.

296
00:36:11,330 --> 00:36:14,380
I couldn't pass through
the first corridor.

297
00:36:15,610 --> 00:36:18,200
If we enter now...

298
00:36:18,310 --> 00:36:20,200
we can't leave silently.

299
00:36:20,320 --> 00:36:22,250
We'll put the conquest at risk.

300
00:36:22,610 --> 00:36:24,600
Then, we'll wait for Osman Bey.

301
00:36:24,800 --> 00:36:28,590
As the war breaks,
we'll use the chaos to enter the dungeon.

302
00:36:29,260 --> 00:36:31,450
What if they come late?

303
00:36:32,060 --> 00:36:34,350
Maybe we should enter now.

304
00:36:35,160 --> 00:36:37,840
We can't do it silently, Ayşe Hatun.

305
00:36:38,270 --> 00:36:40,820
Or we all will die.

306
00:36:43,340 --> 00:36:46,320
If they wanted to kill,
they wouldn't put them in the dungeon.

307
00:36:46,670 --> 00:36:49,090
They'll interrogate them.

308
00:36:49,420 --> 00:36:52,610
As we talked before,
we should get prepared.

309
00:36:52,790 --> 00:36:56,400
When the time comes, we'll
save them from the dungeon.

310
00:37:18,150 --> 00:37:21,740
So, you are Osman's messenger birds.

311
00:37:25,510 --> 00:37:28,360
We came to fight.

312
00:37:30,930 --> 00:37:34,140
I can tell.
You have fought.

313
00:37:35,210 --> 00:37:37,650
Since you are in a dungeon...

314
00:37:40,430 --> 00:37:43,940
so did you. I can tell.

315
00:37:44,220 --> 00:37:46,800
You got shot on your chest!

316
00:37:47,690 --> 00:37:50,360
Now is time for your heart!

317
00:37:59,680 --> 00:38:01,540
Tell me now.

318
00:38:02,840 --> 00:38:05,130
What's Osman's plan?

319
00:38:05,740 --> 00:38:08,590
How many of you are in here?

320
00:38:09,130 --> 00:38:11,930
Akça Dervish.

321
00:38:13,530 --> 00:38:16,440
Kumral Abdal.

322
00:38:16,740 --> 00:38:20,740
And me. Isn't it enough?

323
00:38:22,290 --> 00:38:27,390
Take our heads! Only thing
you'll hear from us...

324
00:38:28,360 --> 00:38:34,080
the soldiers of the righteous
will triumph! You'll lose!

325
00:38:40,120 --> 00:38:46,540
I'll crush you all like bugs!

326
00:38:49,620 --> 00:38:54,630
Until I make you speak,
I'll shatter you.

327
00:38:57,080 --> 00:39:00,160
Search everywhere.
There must be more.

328
00:39:00,340 --> 00:39:02,330
Osman's plans will be ruined.

329
00:39:02,530 --> 00:39:04,310
As you order.

330
00:39:15,080 --> 00:39:17,710
Kumral Abdal, are you alright?

331
00:39:33,190 --> 00:39:36,980
Osman is at our gates with
a formidable force.

332
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:38,870
What will we do?

333
00:39:40,010 --> 00:39:42,530
We'll hand over the city.

334
00:39:45,440 --> 00:39:47,550
Are we giving up, sir?

335
00:39:48,030 --> 00:39:49,610
Never.

336
00:39:51,240 --> 00:39:55,470
Wars aren't always won with
strong soldiers.

337
00:39:57,100 --> 00:40:00,180
Sometimes, you win with
strong traps.

338
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:05,400
When Osman hears that we'll surrender,
he won't attack.

339
00:40:05,940 --> 00:40:08,530
And when he lowers his sword...

340
00:40:09,530 --> 00:40:16,300
we'll destroy him in the center
of Yenişehir.

341
00:40:17,220 --> 00:40:22,490
What if it doesn't work and Osman
still attacks?

342
00:40:22,620 --> 00:40:25,720
He won't. I know Osman.

343
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:28,750
He is food enough to keep his word.

344
00:40:31,530 --> 00:40:36,290
When we surrender the city,
he won't attack.

345
00:40:37,440 --> 00:40:42,050
Sir, what about our honor?

346
00:40:42,220 --> 00:40:45,330
Will we surrender our honor
to win?

347
00:40:52,940 --> 00:40:57,910
Rome is more important than anything.

348
00:40:58,830 --> 00:41:01,760
I can sacrifice everything I have.

349
00:41:03,720 --> 00:41:05,960
Even my honor.

350
00:41:08,660 --> 00:41:10,690
I understand, sir.

351
00:41:13,240 --> 00:41:16,220
Osman Bey's Quarters

352
00:41:19,400 --> 00:41:24,320
The time will be over tomorrow.
If they don't surender...

353
00:41:25,740 --> 00:41:32,700
Turgut Bey, you'll attack to the West.

354
00:41:33,430 --> 00:41:39,720
I will enter from the main gates
at the East.

355
00:41:42,370 --> 00:41:48,330
Aktemur, you'll enter from the North.

356
00:41:49,710 --> 00:41:56,760
The women are inside. Kumral Abdal and
Master Davud have been there for a while.

357
00:41:56,940 --> 00:42:01,780
They'll attack from inside and make
the South open for an attack.

358
00:42:02,160 --> 00:42:06,720
Beys, you'll attack from there.

359
00:42:07,660 --> 00:42:13,060
Inside and outside.
Yenişehir will be ours.

360
00:42:13,210 --> 00:42:14,640
Inshallah.

361
00:42:15,650 --> 00:42:19,600
But we won't touch the people.

362
00:42:20,030 --> 00:42:24,390
Because we will make it home.

363
00:42:25,460 --> 00:42:29,990
Now, everyone should rest.

364
00:42:30,480 --> 00:42:33,300
Tomorrow, the sun will rise for conquest.

365
00:42:34,450 --> 00:42:38,340
With Allah's approval and your
order, my bey.

366
00:42:38,500 --> 00:42:43,360
Thank you. Thank you.
Go on.

367
00:42:59,150 --> 00:43:00,350
Aygül.

368
00:43:01,360 --> 00:43:04,520
Mad girl has gone completely
mad.

369
00:43:04,750 --> 00:43:06,520
Where are we going?

370
00:43:06,690 --> 00:43:09,590
Patience, my Cerkutay.
Patience.

371
00:43:10,000 --> 00:43:14,380
My Cerkutay? I'm getting afraid.

372
00:43:14,630 --> 00:43:19,520
-Aygül where are you taking me?
-How impatient are you?

373
00:43:19,750 --> 00:43:21,460
Come on, move!

374
00:43:22,700 --> 00:43:31,870
Don't you say ''My Aygül, I'll come
to anywhere you want with you''?

375
00:43:32,100 --> 00:43:35,360
I'll come anywhere you want
with you, my Aygül.

376
00:43:36,710 --> 00:43:39,360
As long as we are together.

377
00:43:39,820 --> 00:43:44,320
As long as you are with me.

378
00:43:48,300 --> 00:43:52,420
May Allah not test us with
longing for each other.

379
00:43:53,690 --> 00:43:57,360
Humans come to the world
to be tested.

380
00:43:58,280 --> 00:44:02,450
Allah tests humans with their
most beloved one.

381
00:44:04,030 --> 00:44:11,320
What are you trying to say, mad girl?

382
00:44:25,040 --> 00:44:27,380
Where is this place?

383
00:44:30,690 --> 00:44:34,030
This is our real home.

384
00:44:42,150 --> 00:44:45,690
This is where we'll come together
one day.

385
00:44:50,510 --> 00:44:53,050
We are together, Aygül.

386
00:44:54,660 --> 00:44:57,130
We are married.

387
00:44:58,430 --> 00:45:01,020
We have children.

388
00:45:14,240 --> 00:45:16,740
Aygül, where is this place?

389
00:45:17,270 --> 00:45:20,780
This is where I'll come to.

390
00:45:21,110 --> 00:45:23,480
I'll wait for you here.

391
00:45:44,610 --> 00:45:45,910
No.

392
00:45:47,770 --> 00:45:49,470
No. No!

393
00:45:50,970 --> 00:45:54,870
Aygül! We'll live together.
We'll die together.

394
00:45:55,060 --> 00:45:57,870
Aygül, don't die!
Let's go to our children.

395
00:45:57,980 --> 00:45:59,200
Aygül!

396
00:46:13,940 --> 00:46:15,850
I won't leave you that easily.

397
00:46:15,940 --> 00:46:18,000
No! No!

398
00:46:28,260 --> 00:46:31,530
Not that easily! No!

399
00:46:36,300 --> 00:46:38,020
Aygül!

400
00:46:43,700 --> 00:46:46,270
You'll come too, Cerkutay.

401
00:46:47,820 --> 00:46:49,260
But not now.

402
00:46:51,540 --> 00:46:53,810
We'll unite, Cerkutay.

403
00:46:59,480 --> 00:47:00,820
We'll unite.

404
00:47:01,560 --> 00:47:02,770
Aygül, don't go!

405
00:47:03,280 --> 00:47:04,760
Aygül, don't go!

406
00:47:05,170 --> 00:47:07,140
Don't leave me!

407
00:47:08,450 --> 00:47:10,240
Aygül, don't go!

408
00:47:15,100 --> 00:47:18,230
Aygül, don't go!

409
00:47:19,910 --> 00:47:22,550
Aygül! Aygül!

410
00:47:28,370 --> 00:47:29,780
Aygül!

411
00:47:58,860 --> 00:48:00,370
Cerkutay.

412
00:48:01,020 --> 00:48:03,160
Are you alright?

413
00:48:05,030 --> 00:48:06,750
I was so afraid!

414
00:48:09,670 --> 00:48:11,490
I was so afraid!

415
00:48:12,850 --> 00:48:14,880
Did you see a nightmare?

416
00:48:17,310 --> 00:48:18,860
What did you see?

417
00:48:23,890 --> 00:48:25,530
Nothing!

418
00:48:31,680 --> 00:48:33,160
Nothing!

419
00:48:36,270 --> 00:48:39,170
Nothing! Nothing!

420
00:49:31,380 --> 00:49:32,810
I...

421
00:49:35,640 --> 00:49:37,830
should go and check around.

422
00:49:53,220 --> 00:49:56,540
Ayşe Hatun. It's our time now.

423
00:49:59,250 --> 00:50:05,600
When you put this on their food, they
won't open their eyes for a day.

424
00:50:05,900 --> 00:50:10,050
Thank you, Ayşe Hatun. At least
the troops on the south will sleep.

425
00:50:10,370 --> 00:50:14,630
The rest is ours to kill.

426
00:50:28,400 --> 00:50:33,490
I prepared it last night.
Before the battle.

427
00:50:36,140 --> 00:50:37,300
Come on.

428
00:50:37,780 --> 00:50:41,090
Come on. It's time to renew
our oath.

429
00:50:42,750 --> 00:50:44,440
With Allah's name!

430
00:50:46,790 --> 00:50:48,980
With Allah's name!

431
00:50:49,890 --> 00:50:52,090
With Allah's name!

432
00:50:53,210 --> 00:50:56,910
A weapon and blood fits
a warrior!

433
00:51:00,720 --> 00:51:03,910
Sisters compete with men
to the martyrdom!

434
00:51:04,560 --> 00:51:09,250
Martyrdom is a breath to us,
and jihad is the blood in our veins.

435
00:51:10,500 --> 00:51:14,440
If you are thirsty, satisfy
your heart with jihad.

436
00:51:15,130 --> 00:51:19,340
Sisters, sisters!
They carry the hands of Mother Fatma!

437
00:51:19,640 --> 00:51:24,020
Sisters compete with men
to the martyrdom!

438
00:51:38,800 --> 00:51:41,630
Osman Bey's Quarters

439
00:51:43,530 --> 00:51:47,880
Alps! Alps should be ready like they'll
move at any time.

440
00:51:58,490 --> 00:51:59,760
Salam Alaikum.

441
00:52:00,670 --> 00:52:02,590
Alaikum Salam, my bey.

442
00:52:03,250 --> 00:52:07,220
Sit now. Continue.

443
00:52:07,740 --> 00:52:09,370
What did you do, Balaban?

444
00:52:09,770 --> 00:52:15,670
Boran Bey requested it against
the armored enemies.

445
00:52:18,630 --> 00:52:19,990
-Boran.
-My bey.

446
00:52:20,200 --> 00:52:23,240
Mashallah, you did a good job.

447
00:52:24,000 --> 00:52:25,570
Thank you, my bey.

448
00:52:25,850 --> 00:52:30,290
It'll pierce armors and it'll
get us the city.

449
00:52:31,250 --> 00:52:33,070
Inshallah. Inshallah.

450
00:52:35,390 --> 00:52:36,480
My bey.

451
00:52:38,400 --> 00:52:40,660
News from Romanos' messenger.

452
00:52:41,610 --> 00:52:43,410
Bring him to the tent with
an eyefold.

453
00:52:44,500 --> 00:52:46,730
I'll be coming soon.

454
00:53:10,810 --> 00:53:12,510
Unfold it.

455
00:53:17,350 --> 00:53:18,570
Speak now.

456
00:53:18,920 --> 00:53:21,930
Commander Romanos and the
elders of the city have considered...

457
00:53:22,430 --> 00:53:24,110
and made a decision.

458
00:53:24,810 --> 00:53:28,310
If some conditions are settled,
we are ready to surrender.

459
00:53:30,340 --> 00:53:32,500
What are your conditions?

460
00:53:33,710 --> 00:53:37,190
The people's security of life,
property, and honor will be guaranteed.

461
00:53:37,600 --> 00:53:40,500
The people's faith will not be oppressed.

462
00:53:41,140 --> 00:53:43,590
And Commander Romanos
has a condition.

463
00:53:44,780 --> 00:53:47,490
If his ransom is paid,
he'll be free.

464
00:53:55,260 --> 00:53:57,370
Battle is a wedding to the Turks.

465
00:53:58,190 --> 00:54:03,780
If we decline your conditions,
get in and hang Romanos...

466
00:54:07,430 --> 00:54:09,290
who can stop us?

467
00:54:17,640 --> 00:54:20,720
But we don't have a revenge vendetta.

468
00:54:21,460 --> 00:54:26,330
But we do everything for Allah's words.

469
00:54:29,620 --> 00:54:31,760
I accept your conditions.

470
00:54:32,710 --> 00:54:35,730
Despite his actions, even Romanos
will be free.

471
00:54:37,080 --> 00:54:44,500
Your properties, lives, and dignity
is under my protection.

472
00:54:45,590 --> 00:54:47,160
We are grateful, Osman Bey.

473
00:54:47,700 --> 00:54:51,390
I greet you as the new owner of
Yenişehir.

474
00:55:09,820 --> 00:55:11,300
My bey, what if it's a trap?

475
00:55:11,990 --> 00:55:17,730
So what? We've already taken
our caution.

476
00:55:51,710 --> 00:55:55,580
Aygül, don't! Don't leave me.

477
00:55:55,940 --> 00:55:57,050
Alright?

478
00:55:57,220 --> 00:56:00,610
They said that they'll surrender
but they can't be trusted.

479
00:56:00,740 --> 00:56:01,990
We'll be cautious.

480
00:56:02,070 --> 00:56:03,800
Cerkutay, what do you mean?

481
00:56:03,910 --> 00:56:08,140
You weren't like this even when I
was pregnant. It's not our first battle.

482
00:56:10,180 --> 00:56:12,430
-What is this?
-Henna.

483
00:56:12,880 --> 00:56:15,500
Did you forget it, Cerkutay?
It's a sister tradition.

484
00:56:15,540 --> 00:56:18,550
We sacrifice ourselves to the homeland
before the battle.

485
00:56:20,280 --> 00:56:21,780
Stay beside me!

486
00:56:23,050 --> 00:56:24,540
Come on!

487
00:56:41,070 --> 00:56:43,390
I thought they were surrendering.

488
00:56:43,700 --> 00:56:45,320
What are they doing?

489
00:56:45,440 --> 00:56:48,140
They won't surrender.
It's a trap.

490
00:56:54,520 --> 00:56:56,060
Dishonored!

491
00:56:56,530 --> 00:56:58,690
They have no dignity.

492
00:56:59,170 --> 00:57:02,590
The dungeon is empty.
There are few soldiers.

493
00:57:02,890 --> 00:57:04,970
They are bringing everyone here.

494
00:57:05,420 --> 00:57:08,880
If the soldiers are stacking up,
Osman Bey will be here soon.

495
00:57:10,760 --> 00:57:14,450
Come on, sisters. We'll position
to take out the ones at the roofs.

496
00:57:14,640 --> 00:57:16,460
We'll go to the dungeon with Aygül.

497
00:57:16,460 --> 00:57:19,270
No, I will come with you.

498
00:57:20,100 --> 00:57:24,640
Cerkutay, stay here. Don't you see
all the soldiers?

499
00:57:25,430 --> 00:57:26,730
We'll take care of it.

500
00:57:28,670 --> 00:57:30,340
Cerkutay is right.

501
00:57:32,870 --> 00:57:35,960
Bala, you are pregnant. Cerkutay
should come with you.

502
00:57:36,140 --> 00:57:39,410
Good. Let's go.
May Allah bless our jihad.

503
00:57:44,220 --> 00:57:46,760
Ayşe, you'll come with me.

504
00:57:47,320 --> 00:57:49,410
Alaca, you'll go this way.

505
00:57:49,690 --> 00:57:53,340
Seher, you'll go this way
with the sisters.

506
00:57:53,690 --> 00:57:54,870
Come on.

507
00:57:55,290 --> 00:57:58,140
Keep your arrows at the ready.

508
01:00:16,160 --> 01:00:17,990
Come to me.

509
01:00:34,510 --> 01:00:36,490
Hey, stop!

510
01:00:42,250 --> 01:00:43,660
Where are you headed?

511
01:00:44,830 --> 01:00:47,960
They summoned us from the dungeon
for the woundeds.

512
01:00:48,120 --> 01:00:50,600
You are needed outside.
Get out.

513
01:00:58,040 --> 01:01:00,030
Watch your hand, brother.

514
01:01:04,760 --> 01:01:05,910
Come on.

515
01:01:16,250 --> 01:01:20,070
Cerkutay, you'll take this way
and we'll take that way. Okay?

516
01:01:20,200 --> 01:01:22,870
No.
We'll go together.

517
01:01:23,310 --> 01:01:26,060
Cerkutay what are you talking about?
We don't have time.

518
01:01:26,060 --> 01:01:28,140
We don't know whether
they are alive or not.

519
01:01:28,270 --> 01:01:29,190
Aygul!

520
01:01:29,260 --> 01:01:31,190
Come on Cerkutay!
Go!

521
01:01:35,850 --> 01:01:36,920
My Allah.

522
01:01:38,520 --> 01:01:40,190
Protect my rose.

523
01:01:44,140 --> 01:01:45,530
Aygul!

524
01:01:47,000 --> 01:01:49,400
What happened?
What's going on between you?

525
01:01:51,640 --> 01:01:53,450
He had a nightmare.

526
01:01:54,810 --> 01:01:57,880
He won't tell it,
but he is definitely under its effect.

527
01:01:59,190 --> 01:02:02,790
You said he didn't tell his nightmare.
So how do you know?

528
01:02:04,350 --> 01:02:05,350
Bala...

529
01:02:22,520 --> 01:02:23,590
Bala...

530
01:02:28,670 --> 01:02:30,570
Give me your blessings.

531
01:02:30,970 --> 01:02:32,550
Will you?

532
01:02:40,200 --> 01:02:41,820
I will, my Aygul.

533
01:02:42,910 --> 01:02:44,170
I will.

534
01:02:45,980 --> 01:02:47,710
Give me your blessings too.

535
01:02:49,710 --> 01:02:50,990
I do, Bala.

536
01:02:51,870 --> 01:02:52,990
I do.

537
01:02:54,710 --> 01:02:55,710
Let's go.

538
01:03:04,910 --> 01:03:06,190
Come at once!

539
01:03:06,440 --> 01:03:08,780
I need to get to my Aygul...

540
01:03:08,780 --> 01:03:10,160
...after finishing you.

541
01:03:20,990 --> 01:03:21,990
My Allah...

542
01:03:23,340 --> 01:03:25,550
...don't test me with my sanity.

543
01:03:46,540 --> 01:03:48,510
Hay Masha Allah (praise be)
Bala Hatun!

544
01:03:52,870 --> 01:03:55,180
More power to you, sisters!

545
01:03:55,420 --> 01:03:57,370
Thank Allah we found you safe and sound.

546
01:03:58,780 --> 01:04:01,050
Aygul Hatun, behind you!

547
01:04:04,760 --> 01:04:06,760
I caught you!

548
01:04:34,700 --> 01:04:36,430
Any news from Osman Bey?

549
01:04:37,110 --> 01:04:38,950
He is fine.
He is on his way.

550
01:04:38,950 --> 01:04:42,180
Everyone get back to their missions
just like how we talked before.

551
01:04:42,180 --> 01:04:43,320
Osman Bey is waiting!

552
01:04:43,320 --> 01:04:44,270
Let's go!

553
01:04:45,160 --> 01:04:46,360
Master Davut.

554
01:04:46,830 --> 01:04:49,530
Your weapons are waiting for you
at the end of the hall.

555
01:04:51,630 --> 01:04:53,290
They are on fire!

556
01:05:06,750 --> 01:05:09,130
We are face to face again, Osman.

557
01:05:17,050 --> 01:05:19,480
This is going to be our last meeting.

558
01:05:22,890 --> 01:05:23,870
Right.

559
01:05:29,710 --> 01:05:30,750
You defeated me.

560
01:05:35,720 --> 01:05:38,810
You defeated the army of Rome.

561
01:06:45,670 --> 01:06:48,200
Now deliver Yenisehir to me.

562
01:06:49,830 --> 01:06:51,530
So that no one dies.

563
01:06:54,950 --> 01:07:00,010
And Kayi will control here from now on.

564
01:07:19,630 --> 01:07:21,470
Do I have any other option?

565
01:07:58,760 --> 01:08:01,220
I will scratch your eyes out if
you betray my Bey!

566
01:08:01,400 --> 01:08:02,630
Sisters!

567
01:08:05,130 --> 01:08:07,230
What's happening?
What is happening?

568
01:08:07,230 --> 01:08:08,680
O Haqq!

569
01:08:22,350 --> 01:08:24,060
O Haqq!

570
01:08:30,680 --> 01:08:32,710
Masha Allah (praise be)
to my Hatun.

571
01:08:39,899 --> 01:08:42,109
Allah is eternal!

572
01:08:50,200 --> 01:08:51,479
Push it, brothers.

573
01:08:52,700 --> 01:08:53,770
Let's push.

574
01:08:55,149 --> 01:08:56,700
Push, brother!

575
01:08:56,910 --> 01:09:00,569
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

576
01:09:14,140 --> 01:09:16,729
Hit them, valiants!
For the sake of Allah!

577
01:09:51,470 --> 01:09:52,580
Come on.

578
01:10:03,340 --> 01:10:07,450
Yenisehir will be Turks' land.

579
01:10:09,080 --> 01:10:11,640
Inshallah(if Allah permits), Master Davut.

580
01:10:11,910 --> 01:10:15,110
Let's go.
Our brothers are fighting.

581
01:10:15,690 --> 01:10:17,110
Let's go.

582
01:10:25,180 --> 01:10:30,080
You are the new commander, Master Davut.

583
01:10:30,360 --> 01:10:32,220
It's not time to talk, Kumral.

584
01:10:32,380 --> 01:10:34,910
Let your hands work
instead of your tongue.

585
01:10:35,130 --> 01:10:36,540
Come on.

586
01:10:36,910 --> 01:10:38,780
Let's set them on fire.

587
01:10:38,780 --> 01:10:41,370
We won't die before doing it.

588
01:10:41,480 --> 01:10:43,870
- Let's go!
- Allah is eternal!

589
01:11:03,830 --> 01:11:07,100
We won't stop until we become a martyr!

590
01:11:11,690 --> 01:11:16,780
We won't stop until we plant our flag
in the center of the town!

591
01:11:58,440 --> 01:12:00,170
Bala! Come on!

592
01:12:01,720 --> 01:12:03,020
Come on!

593
01:12:03,020 --> 01:12:06,640
Allah is eternal!
Allah is eternal!

594
01:12:11,900 --> 01:12:18,990
Allah is eternal!
Allah is eternal!

595
01:12:23,640 --> 01:12:25,210
Masha Allah!
(praise be)

596
01:12:25,350 --> 01:12:26,830
Wolves are on the duty!

597
01:12:26,830 --> 01:12:29,500
What do you think, Cerkutay?
This is Kayi tribe!

598
01:12:29,500 --> 01:12:31,260
Which gates can stop us?

599
01:12:31,350 --> 01:12:33,180
Allah is eternal!

600
01:12:33,230 --> 01:12:35,520
You are an army on your own, my Hatun.

601
01:12:35,550 --> 01:12:36,750
Allah is righteous!

602
01:12:36,750 --> 01:12:39,320
- Allah is eternal!
- Allah is righteous!

603
01:13:58,920 --> 01:14:00,590
Romanos.

604
01:14:45,010 --> 01:14:46,340
Kumral!

605
01:15:50,090 --> 01:15:51,830
Come on Master Davut!

606
01:15:59,270 --> 01:16:00,490
Are you fine, Master Davut?

607
01:16:03,420 --> 01:16:04,710
Are you wounded?

608
01:16:07,690 --> 01:16:09,500
Come on.
Come on!

609
01:16:10,010 --> 01:16:10,840
Come on!

610
01:16:23,430 --> 01:16:24,760
What are you looking for.

611
01:16:25,830 --> 01:16:28,590
You have nowhere to run, you infidel.

612
01:16:29,770 --> 01:16:31,800
Let's see how brave you are now.

613
01:16:51,400 --> 01:16:54,220
Take that dog.
Don't kill him.

614
01:16:55,910 --> 01:16:57,230
Now!

615
01:17:06,830 --> 01:17:08,060
Malhun.

616
01:17:09,180 --> 01:17:10,440
Come on Hatuns.

617
01:17:10,560 --> 01:17:12,230
May our fight be blessed.

618
01:17:12,830 --> 01:17:14,090
Come on.

619
01:17:36,590 --> 01:17:38,230
Ayse!
Come on!

620
01:17:56,620 --> 01:17:58,030
Stop him!

621
01:18:32,690 --> 01:18:34,310
Ayse!

622
01:18:40,030 --> 01:18:41,210
Come on!

623
01:19:37,150 --> 01:19:40,300
Do not try for nothing, Kumral.

624
01:19:43,370 --> 01:19:48,540
I got ahead of you.
I will become a martyr first.

625
01:19:49,980 --> 01:19:51,230
No way.

626
01:19:52,910 --> 01:19:55,470
You can't leave as you wish,
Master Davut.

627
01:19:56,110 --> 01:19:58,630
We will have many wars to fight.

628
01:19:59,560 --> 01:20:01,240
Hold on, Master Davut.

629
01:20:01,750 --> 01:20:03,660
You'll be fine Inshallah.

630
01:20:10,470 --> 01:20:15,390
Am I going to die in
a foreign land, Kumral?

631
01:20:16,940 --> 01:20:19,560
Have we conquered yet?

632
01:20:22,830 --> 01:20:23,830
Yes.

633
01:20:25,550 --> 01:20:27,320
All our alps are inside.

634
01:20:30,470 --> 01:20:31,910
Thank Allah.

635
01:20:38,880 --> 01:20:42,030
Give me your blessings.

636
01:20:43,950 --> 01:20:45,960
I do, Master Davut.

637
01:20:46,780 --> 01:20:48,150
I do.

638
01:20:48,430 --> 01:20:53,830
"I bear witness that
there is no deity but, Allah...

639
01:20:57,430 --> 01:21:06,770
and I bear witness that Muhammad
is the messenger of Allah”.

640
01:21:13,660 --> 01:21:18,550
"Verily we belong to Allah
and verily to him do we return."

641
01:21:21,730 --> 01:21:24,380
My brother is a martyr now.

642
01:21:44,180 --> 01:21:47,520
Come to me, ignobles!
Come to me so I can send you to hell!

643
01:21:56,140 --> 01:21:58,030
Are you trying to die, mad girl?

644
01:21:58,030 --> 01:21:59,840
Didn't I tell you to stay with me?

645
01:21:59,840 --> 01:22:01,540
I do what you do, mad boy.

646
01:22:01,600 --> 01:22:04,580
I fight for our children, grandchildren!

647
01:22:07,460 --> 01:22:09,790
You won't fight
without me!

648
01:22:13,070 --> 01:22:17,800
Either we live together
or we die together.

649
01:22:19,520 --> 01:22:21,300
Inshallah (if Allah permits).

650
01:22:33,470 --> 01:22:34,840
I had a nightmare.

651
01:22:39,980 --> 01:22:41,650
Cerkutay!

652
01:22:43,650 --> 01:22:45,710
Aygul!

653
01:22:47,140 --> 01:22:48,070
Aygul.

654
01:22:54,300 --> 01:22:56,260
Aygul, Aygul!

655
01:23:13,750 --> 01:23:14,980
Cerkutay!

656
01:23:32,500 --> 01:23:34,500
I wanted to settle down.

657
01:23:35,710 --> 01:23:37,400
They stopped me.

658
01:23:38,540 --> 01:23:43,700
I loved a rose.
I loved Aygul* (Ay=moon Gul=rose)

659
01:23:43,770 --> 01:23:46,050
They broke her.

660
01:23:46,180 --> 01:23:52,990
Now what's left in my hand
except for berserk?

661
01:24:22,080 --> 01:24:24,000
Did you shoot with this hand?

662
01:24:39,400 --> 01:24:41,600
Did you aim with those eyes?

663
01:25:12,380 --> 01:25:13,720
Aygul.

664
01:25:15,040 --> 01:25:19,440
Aygul!
Aygul!

665
01:25:21,610 --> 01:25:23,200
Cerkutay.

666
01:25:27,880 --> 01:25:29,900
Are you fine?

667
01:25:30,370 --> 01:25:33,130
I am, I am, Aygul.

668
01:25:39,080 --> 01:25:42,150
Rose of my moon, hold on.
(Ay means moon, gul means rose in Turkish)

669
01:25:42,150 --> 01:25:46,880
Do not cry Cerkutay.

670
01:25:49,770 --> 01:25:51,060
Don't.

671
01:26:36,630 --> 01:26:37,930
Come on
Come on

672
01:26:41,060 --> 01:26:43,200
Romanos.

673
01:26:50,210 --> 01:26:52,970
I won't die before killing you, Osman.

674
01:26:53,770 --> 01:26:56,460
There is no such sword
to kill me.

675
01:26:57,290 --> 01:26:58,930
Come to me.

676
01:27:10,410 --> 01:27:11,890
Where are you Aygul?

677
01:27:44,610 --> 01:27:49,760
The sword to kill you is in my hands.

678
01:27:51,220 --> 01:27:52,250
Someday...

679
01:27:55,820 --> 01:27:58,330
...you'll breed will vanish.

680
01:27:59,120 --> 01:28:08,560
Both you and your breed will die.

681
01:28:25,430 --> 01:28:30,050
We're all going to die, but...

682
01:28:30,740 --> 01:28:33,450
...Turks' state will stay forever.

683
01:29:14,820 --> 01:29:17,090
Take that dog's head.

684
01:29:25,220 --> 01:29:27,740
Thank my Creator!

685
01:29:32,940 --> 01:29:34,570
Thanks a lot.

686
01:29:36,650 --> 01:29:38,400
Thank you, Creator!

687
01:29:44,810 --> 01:29:46,080
Thank Him.

688
01:29:48,570 --> 01:29:52,170
Valiants, I appreciate your bravery!

689
01:29:53,420 --> 01:29:58,000
Thank Allah.
Thank Allah

690
01:29:59,570 --> 01:30:00,980
Thank Allah.

691
01:30:01,440 --> 01:30:04,810
Thank you, Osman Bey. You made this city
a homeland to Turks, to us.

692
01:30:04,810 --> 01:30:09,290
No, we took the homeland from our
ancestors.

693
01:30:09,290 --> 01:30:17,260
But those who will enlarge it are our
children.

694
01:30:18,250 --> 01:30:19,260
Son...

695
01:30:21,940 --> 01:30:23,570
...draw your sword.

696
01:30:24,460 --> 01:30:27,040
This won't go down until the world is
ours, my Bey!

697
01:30:27,040 --> 01:30:29,040
Praise be!

698
01:30:31,040 --> 01:30:32,930
Praise be!

699
01:30:36,580 --> 01:30:38,290
-My Bey.
-Valiants.

700
01:30:43,170 --> 01:30:46,930
Romanos convinced the people of
disobedience.

701
01:30:47,180 --> 01:30:49,610
They neither speak nor surrender.

702
01:30:57,530 --> 01:30:59,570
They didn't let us close, my Bey.

703
01:30:59,570 --> 01:31:01,570
We didn't make a move without your
order.

704
01:31:03,330 --> 01:31:04,700
What should we do, my Bey?

705
01:31:05,690 --> 01:31:09,320
So, they paint us badly.

706
01:31:12,480 --> 01:31:17,640
In that case, it is time to show them
the truth.

707
01:31:18,410 --> 01:31:21,930
They won't believe us, my Bey.
They are afraid.

708
01:31:22,730 --> 01:31:23,930
Right.

709
01:31:27,700 --> 01:31:30,010
Is the Priest here?

710
01:31:30,010 --> 01:31:31,090
He is, my Bey.

711
01:31:32,010 --> 01:31:34,260
Since they don't believe us...

712
01:31:35,480 --> 01:31:37,940
...one of them will speak then.

713
01:31:39,380 --> 01:31:41,360
Call the Priest.

714
01:31:42,200 --> 01:31:44,940
Gather everyone in the square.

715
01:31:44,940 --> 01:31:46,770
-Yes, my Bey.
-Come on.

716
01:31:57,420 --> 01:31:58,810
Why?

717
01:32:00,400 --> 01:32:02,140
Why did you do this?

718
01:32:03,690 --> 01:32:08,040
Father is a mountain, Cerkutay.

719
01:32:10,810 --> 01:32:15,170
A child can't be without a father.

720
01:32:16,520 --> 01:32:22,740
So that you be a mountain to our children.

721
01:32:23,380 --> 01:32:27,660
No! No! No! I told you!

722
01:32:27,660 --> 01:32:31,850
We will either live together or die
together.

723
01:32:33,370 --> 01:32:35,880
No, Aygül! No!

724
01:32:35,880 --> 01:32:38,690
You will get up now and we will go to
Kumral Abdal.

725
01:32:38,730 --> 01:32:40,330
He will treat you.

726
01:32:40,330 --> 01:32:50,260
Cerkutay, do you remember the dream you
had?

727
01:32:52,480 --> 01:32:55,770
I dreamed that too.

728
01:32:59,500 --> 01:33:04,880
I saw where I am going, Cerkutay.

729
01:33:05,690 --> 01:33:11,900
No, no! Don't leave me without you!

730
01:33:13,810 --> 01:33:20,720
Don't talk like death is the end,
Cerkutay.

731
01:33:25,720 --> 01:33:29,810
We will meet in the afterlife.

732
01:33:33,320 --> 01:33:34,680
I will wait.

733
01:33:36,400 --> 01:33:37,850
I will wait.

734
01:33:39,970 --> 01:33:46,330
But don't come early, come in time.

735
01:33:46,380 --> 01:33:53,660
Don't go, Aygül! Don't go, Aygül!
Don't go, Aygül!

736
01:33:54,170 --> 01:34:02,200
I bear witness that there is no god
but Allah, and I bear witness...

737
01:34:02,680 --> 01:34:17,370
...that Muhammad (PBUH) is the
servant and Messenger of Allah.

738
01:34:36,520 --> 01:34:47,440
Aygül! Mad girl!
Aygül! Mad girl!

739
01:34:59,750 --> 01:35:01,180
Aygül!

740
01:35:06,420 --> 01:35:09,810
Wake up! Wake up!

741
01:35:12,720 --> 01:35:18,700
Aygül! Aygül!

742
01:35:42,640 --> 01:35:43,800
I don't want it!

743
01:35:47,360 --> 01:35:50,300
I don't want it! We will never surrender!

744
01:36:23,600 --> 01:36:28,320
Children, children.

745
01:36:55,010 --> 01:37:01,060
Come here. Come here boy!

746
01:37:13,880 --> 01:37:15,120
Son.

747
01:37:23,480 --> 01:37:25,130
People!

748
01:37:28,770 --> 01:37:30,260
Come here!

749
01:37:34,170 --> 01:37:36,840
Come here!

750
01:37:43,000 --> 01:37:51,960
We didn't come here to kill, on the
contrary, we came to make it live!

751
01:37:53,800 --> 01:37:56,570
We had never drawn our swords at an
innococent!

752
01:37:58,360 --> 01:38:00,330
And we never will!

753
01:38:03,640 --> 01:38:08,080
We had never made a child cry.

754
01:38:08,690 --> 01:38:10,530
And we won't!

755
01:38:16,060 --> 01:38:23,180
You are the same as Söğüt and İnegöl
people to me.

756
01:38:28,080 --> 01:38:32,100
Come on, son. Go to your mother.

757
01:38:32,100 --> 01:38:34,100
Come on.

758
01:38:35,280 --> 01:38:36,680
Come on, go.

759
01:38:41,610 --> 01:38:44,260
Your places of worship will be repaired.

760
01:38:44,880 --> 01:38:48,370
You will continue your trade.

761
01:38:48,370 --> 01:38:54,200
And your properties will still be yours.

762
01:38:54,200 --> 01:38:56,690
No one will touch them.

763
01:38:59,160 --> 01:39:01,410
I know your taxes are expensive.

764
01:39:03,240 --> 01:39:04,980
We will decrease them as well.

765
01:39:05,940 --> 01:39:10,880
Your lives and your properties are
entrusted to me from now on.

766
01:39:20,570 --> 01:39:29,160
But if there are still people who have
doubts and fear me...

767
01:39:33,970 --> 01:39:36,420
...you can ask the Priest about us.

768
01:39:39,660 --> 01:39:44,080
He is your co-religionist and religious
leader.

769
01:39:44,730 --> 01:39:49,200
He knows you and you know him.

770
01:39:50,520 --> 01:39:53,290
You can open your hearts to him freely.

771
01:39:56,040 --> 01:39:58,140
There you go.

772
01:40:00,540 --> 01:40:01,820
Alps.

773
01:40:03,330 --> 01:40:04,320
Come on.

774
01:40:14,800 --> 01:40:17,780
May Jesus be with you my sisters and
brothers.

775
01:40:19,680 --> 01:40:21,360
I understand your fears.

776
01:40:22,320 --> 01:40:28,500
However, I witnessed every word of Osman
Bey.

777
01:40:30,410 --> 01:40:33,101
Giving up the city is the best for you.

778
01:40:34,560 --> 01:40:37,190
And later on, trusting me.

779
01:40:38,770 --> 01:40:43,630
You will see nothing in your city except
justice and mercy.

780
01:40:44,580 --> 01:40:46,040
I assure you.

781
01:40:56,320 --> 01:40:57,920
Master Davut.

782
01:41:03,570 --> 01:41:04,970
Master Davut.

783
01:41:14,450 --> 01:41:16,730
The architect of many conquests...

784
01:41:24,450 --> 01:41:26,280
...now...

785
01:41:27,680 --> 01:41:30,160
...became a martyr in the land of Turk.

786
01:41:37,750 --> 01:41:39,470
May his martyrdom be blessed.

787
01:41:39,540 --> 01:41:41,790
-Amen!
-Amen!

788
01:41:42,930 --> 01:41:47,390
His name will go on as long as the lands
of Turks...

789
01:41:48,220 --> 01:41:50,190
...exist.

790
01:42:16,360 --> 01:42:18,280
Cerkutay!

791
01:42:34,810 --> 01:42:36,210
Aygül!

792
01:43:11,760 --> 01:43:13,180
Aygül!

793
01:44:20,410 --> 01:44:22,640
What will I do now?

794
01:44:47,520 --> 01:44:49,060
Cerkutay.

795
01:47:30,170 --> 01:47:32,210
-Amen.
-Amen.

796
01:47:35,570 --> 01:47:36,570
Amen.

797
01:47:49,380 --> 01:47:50,930
Raise your head.

798
01:47:52,470 --> 01:47:53,710
Raise your head.

799
01:47:55,630 --> 01:47:59,300
This is neither an end nor a defeat.

800
01:48:03,530 --> 01:48:07,480
This is a new beginning for all of us.

801
01:48:15,710 --> 01:48:16,930
People!

802
01:48:18,990 --> 01:48:24,590
Yeni Şehir will be the capital of Kayı
from now on!

803
01:48:25,980 --> 01:48:29,570
Together we will restore these lands
where the hearts of Turks...

804
01:48:29,890 --> 01:48:32,010
...and Islam will beat.

805
01:48:33,420 --> 01:48:37,070
Therefore, your life...

806
01:48:37,880 --> 01:48:39,320
... your property...

807
01:48:40,040 --> 01:48:41,600
...and your honor...

808
01:48:43,470 --> 01:48:44,960
...are entrusted to me!

809
01:48:48,770 --> 01:48:52,350
A state is founded on Justice.

810
01:48:52,840 --> 01:48:55,330
And as long as there is justice...

811
01:48:56,350 --> 01:48:58,160
...the state will remain.

812
01:49:00,470 --> 01:49:04,470
Thus, your rights are also entrusted to
us.

813
01:49:06,490 --> 01:49:09,710
You will live in prosperity without
discrimination of religion...

814
01:49:10,100 --> 01:49:12,150
...and nationality.

815
01:49:12,480 --> 01:49:17,120
But know that...

816
01:49:17,800 --> 01:49:20,050
...I am not your owner.

817
01:49:21,150 --> 01:49:23,520
I am only...

818
01:49:24,010 --> 01:49:26,660
...the owner of the sword of justice.

819
01:49:29,940 --> 01:49:32,550
When I become dust one day...

820
01:49:33,960 --> 01:49:36,900
...what will remain will be my poor tent
...

821
01:49:37,000 --> 01:49:38,910
...my wretched horse...

822
01:49:41,010 --> 01:49:43,970
...and my sword that dispenses justice.

823
01:49:45,110 --> 01:49:47,410
We don't forget where we came from...

824
01:49:48,260 --> 01:49:49,910
...and why.

825
01:49:51,260 --> 01:49:55,930
But we always keep in mind where we
are going.

826
01:49:58,640 --> 01:50:00,680
Our way is the way of Allah.

827
01:50:01,160 --> 01:50:04,130
It is the world order that leads us to
that path.

828
01:50:04,920 --> 01:50:09,080
Where the road takes us is the word
of Allah.

829
01:50:11,560 --> 01:50:14,610
We must make moves for that road.

830
01:50:15,370 --> 01:50:16,960
We must take action.

831
01:50:18,290 --> 01:50:24,330
Just like how our ancestors came to these
lands and made them a home...

832
01:50:25,150 --> 01:50:26,570
...we will do the same.

833
01:50:28,810 --> 01:50:30,520
We will walk towards the future.

834
01:50:32,570 --> 01:50:34,740
Our next home will be...

835
01:50:35,660 --> 01:50:37,400
...Yeni Şehir.

836
01:50:41,070 --> 01:50:45,280
Yeni Şehir will open many doors of
conquest for us.

837
01:50:46,940 --> 01:50:49,170
It will make us dominate the world.

838
01:50:51,010 --> 01:50:54,920
Time is like a river, it flows.

839
01:50:55,640 --> 01:50:59,730
We will be the bed of that river.

840
01:51:01,070 --> 01:51:03,950
We will build a state that will last
forever.

841
01:51:06,660 --> 01:51:08,850
It will be such a state that it will...

842
01:51:09,310 --> 01:51:14,120
...fly the flag of Islam around the whole
world.

843
01:51:14,740 --> 01:51:16,790
It will be such a state that it will...

844
01:51:17,200 --> 01:51:20,730
...spread justice to the whole world.

845
01:51:22,390 --> 01:51:24,100
It will be such a state that...

846
01:51:25,270 --> 01:51:27,320
....it will always remain!

847
01:51:30,260 --> 01:51:32,530
-Allah is one!

848
01:51:51,430 --> 01:51:53,510
Allah is one!

849
01:51:59,640 --> 01:52:01,870
I brought Osman Bey's greetings, Ali Bey.

850
01:52:02,890 --> 01:52:05,120
Thank you!

851
01:52:07,150 --> 01:52:08,890
I am glad you came, valiant.

852
01:52:12,320 --> 01:52:14,470
We could thankfully conquer Yeni Şehir.

853
01:52:14,660 --> 01:52:16,470
Osman Bey is having a feast.

854
01:52:16,550 --> 01:52:17,720
He expects you too.

855
01:52:18,030 --> 01:52:19,330
Praise be!

856
01:52:19,950 --> 01:52:21,670
Such blessed news!

857
01:52:22,970 --> 01:52:27,610
Right! Osman Bey doesn't know how to
stop.

858
01:52:28,760 --> 01:52:30,940
Praise be! Praise be!

859
01:52:32,900 --> 01:52:36,960
We are honored to accept Osman Bey's
invitation.

860
01:52:37,370 --> 01:52:41,700
Tell him that we will come, valiant.

861
01:52:42,480 --> 01:52:43,610
Thank you.

862
01:52:53,640 --> 01:52:56,210
Oh, my Allah, mightiest of all!

863
01:52:56,250 --> 01:53:00,900
You granted us many conquests.

864
01:53:02,480 --> 01:53:05,150
On this land you granted us...

865
01:53:06,790 --> 01:53:08,870
...many valiants and many sisters...

866
01:53:10,470 --> 01:53:13,070
...bled.

867
01:53:16,510 --> 01:53:17,760
Gündüz Bey!

868
01:53:24,910 --> 01:53:26,050
Osman!

869
01:53:26,080 --> 01:53:27,360
Mother!

870
01:53:28,240 --> 01:53:29,980
-Mother!
-Mother!

871
01:53:30,190 --> 01:53:31,990
Göktuğ!

872
01:53:34,880 --> 01:53:36,490
Cerkutay!

873
01:53:51,810 --> 01:53:55,860
I bear witness that there is no god
but Allah, and I bear witness that...

874
01:53:56,050 --> 01:54:00,520
...Muhammad (PBUH) is the servant
and Messenger of Allah.

875
01:54:02,540 --> 01:54:04,200
My Allah you order in your book...

876
01:54:10,600 --> 01:54:13,500
...not to call the martyrs dead.

877
01:54:17,120 --> 01:54:24,270
May you keep our martyrs together with
our prophets and your good servants.

878
01:54:25,630 --> 01:54:31,950
Accept them into your heaven with those
who were martyred in Badr and Uhud.

879
01:54:38,900 --> 01:54:40,200
Amen.

880
01:54:42,900 --> 01:54:44,150
Amen.

881
01:54:53,150 --> 01:54:54,230
Sons.

882
01:55:03,400 --> 01:55:05,230
We have something to tell you, father.

883
01:55:19,300 --> 01:55:20,290
First Selvi...

884
01:55:20,670 --> 01:55:21,650
...now Aygül.

885
01:55:23,630 --> 01:55:25,290
I don't know which one to cry for.

886
01:55:27,310 --> 01:55:31,210
My sister died before finding out what the
traitor she called her husband had done.

887
01:55:31,740 --> 01:55:33,730
It wouldn't be better if she did, Malhun.

888
01:55:34,640 --> 01:55:36,380
She would have gotten worse.

889
01:55:37,690 --> 01:55:40,220
Every cloud has a silver lining.

890
01:55:41,260 --> 01:55:44,070
Maybe this was better for her.

891
01:55:44,820 --> 01:55:46,050
Right.

892
01:55:47,010 --> 01:55:48,930
Selvi, Aygül...

893
01:55:49,460 --> 01:55:50,500
...Gonca.

894
01:55:50,630 --> 01:55:52,970
And many other sisters who were martyred.

895
01:55:53,810 --> 01:55:55,150
They walked to Allah...

896
01:55:55,530 --> 01:55:56,700
...for a blessed cause.

897
01:55:58,630 --> 01:55:59,630
My Aygül knew...

898
01:56:00,200 --> 01:56:02,810
...where she was going before.

899
01:56:06,730 --> 01:56:07,840
But...

900
01:56:08,480 --> 01:56:11,060
...how will we tell this to her children?

901
01:56:12,330 --> 01:56:13,940
We will be strong, my Ayşe.

902
01:56:14,240 --> 01:56:15,470
We will be strong.

903
01:56:17,050 --> 01:56:20,890
Let's not cry for them anymore and
make them uneasy.

904
01:56:24,030 --> 01:56:25,090
Hatuns.

905
01:56:27,560 --> 01:56:29,980
Didn't we risk dying on our cause's way...

906
01:56:30,650 --> 01:56:33,220
...the first day we laid our hands on our
swords?

907
01:56:36,530 --> 01:56:38,920
Didn't we get these hennas for this
reason?

908
01:56:41,450 --> 01:56:42,650
Now...

909
01:56:43,880 --> 01:56:45,750
...we send our blessings...

910
01:56:46,000 --> 01:56:48,820
...to every martyr who opened the way
for the conquest.

911
01:56:49,720 --> 01:56:50,890
Amen.

912
01:57:41,970 --> 01:57:43,690
Allah is one.

913
01:57:45,980 --> 01:57:47,850
Allah is one.

914
01:57:50,830 --> 01:57:51,940
Allah is one.

915
01:57:55,470 --> 01:57:57,620
Allah is one.

916
01:58:07,470 --> 01:58:09,420
May peace be upon you.

917
01:58:12,410 --> 01:58:14,300
May peace be upon you.

918
01:58:18,070 --> 01:58:19,660
My Rabb.

919
01:58:41,690 --> 01:58:43,560
In the name of Allah.

920
01:58:44,710 --> 01:58:46,230
Here you go sons.

921
01:58:47,360 --> 01:58:48,940
Enjoy.

922
01:58:59,770 --> 01:59:01,470
Yes, sons.

923
01:59:03,110 --> 01:59:04,250
Tell me.

924
01:59:05,670 --> 01:59:06,730
My Bey father.

925
01:59:07,050 --> 01:59:09,130
We thought of something with Alaaddin.

926
01:59:09,630 --> 01:59:11,870
But first, we ask for your blessing.

927
01:59:17,270 --> 01:59:18,330
Tell me.

928
01:59:18,630 --> 01:59:21,360
We learned that a state is established
in hardships.

929
01:59:22,360 --> 01:59:24,990
But they go down because of wars
for the throne...

930
01:59:25,230 --> 01:59:27,870
...jealousies and evil.

931
01:59:30,020 --> 01:59:33,140
Thus, we want to be the two wings
of the state you'll establish.

932
01:59:33,140 --> 01:59:34,820
We want to remain together, father.

933
01:59:37,540 --> 01:59:38,750
If you'll let me...

934
01:59:39,020 --> 01:59:41,770
...I'd like to serve the state with my
knowledge.

935
01:59:42,510 --> 01:59:45,690
And for this, I want to go to Konya.
To a madrasa.

936
01:59:46,600 --> 01:59:47,950
My Alaaddin!

937
01:59:48,920 --> 01:59:51,810
Praise be! Praise be!

938
01:59:53,150 --> 01:59:54,480
What about you, my Orhan?

939
01:59:54,840 --> 01:59:56,380
I want to fight by your side.

940
01:59:56,770 --> 01:59:58,970
I want to have your back with my sword,
father.

941
02:00:04,720 --> 02:00:05,870
So...

942
02:00:06,600 --> 02:00:07,710
...sons...

943
02:00:08,170 --> 02:00:10,460
...you want to rule together.

944
02:00:11,130 --> 02:00:12,230
Just like...

945
02:00:12,930 --> 02:00:15,040
...Kültigin and Bilge Khan.

946
02:00:19,680 --> 02:00:21,530
Praise be to my valiants!

947
02:00:22,060 --> 02:00:23,400
Praise be!

948
02:00:25,520 --> 02:00:26,580
Now...

949
02:00:28,120 --> 02:00:29,410
...listen to me carefully.

950
02:00:31,490 --> 02:00:32,640
Sons...

951
02:00:34,350 --> 02:00:37,580
... a state is a two-winged bird.

952
02:00:38,740 --> 02:00:40,380
One of the wings is a sword...

953
02:00:41,330 --> 02:00:44,380
...and the other is knowledge and wisdom.

954
02:00:45,890 --> 02:00:47,000
But...

955
02:00:47,540 --> 02:00:49,820
...if one of these wings is missing...

956
02:00:50,670 --> 02:00:52,310
...this bird can't fly.

957
02:00:52,720 --> 02:00:56,320
How can a bird that can't fly rule
the world?

958
02:00:58,610 --> 02:01:00,710
How can it spread justice to the world?

959
02:01:03,260 --> 02:01:04,330
Sons...

960
02:01:05,960 --> 02:01:08,520
...you are the two wings of that bird.

961
02:01:09,190 --> 02:01:10,770
The state will live with you.

962
02:01:13,350 --> 02:01:15,490
And you will live with the state.

963
02:01:18,870 --> 02:01:20,140
My lions!

964
02:01:24,850 --> 02:01:28,010
İnegöl Castle

965
02:01:46,170 --> 02:01:47,630
I came, Gündüz.

966
02:01:49,380 --> 02:01:50,900
You might say it is late.

967
02:01:53,930 --> 02:01:55,150
Of course, you are right.

968
02:01:59,680 --> 02:02:01,370
I couldn't come before.

969
02:02:15,850 --> 02:02:17,250
Now I came.

970
02:02:23,450 --> 02:02:24,610
Ayşe!

971
02:02:24,810 --> 02:02:25,910
Gündüz!

972
02:02:31,670 --> 02:02:33,370
I came to say what
I couldn't say...

973
02:02:34,960 --> 02:02:36,600
...to your face.

974
02:02:38,100 --> 02:02:40,890
I didn't bury only you in this land,
Gündüz.

975
02:02:43,440 --> 02:02:45,150
I buried my Işık too.

976
02:02:49,570 --> 02:02:51,130
I was in the dark.

977
02:02:53,200 --> 02:02:54,230
I couldn't speak.

978
02:02:57,290 --> 02:03:02,280
Every day became night since you left.

979
02:03:04,810 --> 02:03:06,200
But I won't cry.

980
02:03:08,040 --> 02:03:11,610
You told me not to. So, I won't cry.

981
02:03:18,980 --> 02:03:20,350
But now.

982
02:03:26,050 --> 02:03:27,680
The sun is rising again.

983
02:03:30,140 --> 02:03:31,290
Again.

984
02:03:31,970 --> 02:03:33,150
Gündüz.

985
02:03:34,370 --> 02:03:35,810
Gündüz Bey.

986
02:03:36,370 --> 02:03:38,340
We are having another child.

987
02:03:41,080 --> 02:03:42,940
Another child from you...

988
02:03:43,650 --> 02:03:44,930
...to me.

989
02:03:46,590 --> 02:03:48,110
But without you...

990
02:03:49,850 --> 02:03:51,190
...longing for you...

991
02:03:59,790 --> 02:04:03,100
You were so happy when you found out I was
pregnant with Aktemur.

992
02:04:04,050 --> 02:04:06,100
Your eyes smiled at me.

993
02:04:08,620 --> 02:04:12,990
I wish you were here with me now
so that...

994
02:04:14,950 --> 02:04:17,960
...I could tell you these while looking
at your pretty eyes.

995
02:04:19,830 --> 02:04:21,010
And you would tell me...

996
02:04:25,090 --> 02:04:30,670
...''My Ayşe, light of my eye.''

997
02:04:30,940 --> 02:04:32,910
I couldn't save you, Gündüz!

998
02:04:33,880 --> 02:04:35,720
I couldn't save you.

999
02:04:36,110 --> 02:04:38,120
I couldn't save you.

1000
02:04:39,680 --> 02:04:40,810
No.

1001
02:04:42,760 --> 02:04:44,590
Don't think I am ungrateful.

1002
02:04:44,870 --> 02:04:46,050
Could I ever be?

1003
02:04:46,270 --> 02:04:47,390
No.

1004
02:04:47,990 --> 02:04:48,950
No.

1005
02:04:50,360 --> 02:04:51,540
You...

1006
02:04:54,380 --> 02:04:56,590
...made İnegöl home for us.

1007
02:04:57,680 --> 02:04:58,910
You died for us.

1008
02:05:01,000 --> 02:05:05,130
I will raise children who will take care
of your legacy.

1009
02:05:08,050 --> 02:05:09,580
Gündüz Bey's sons...

1010
02:05:10,160 --> 02:05:11,930
...will be befitting Gündüz Bey.

1011
02:05:30,810 --> 02:05:31,790
My Malhun.

1012
02:05:32,990 --> 02:05:34,490
Thanks to Allah that...

1013
02:05:35,780 --> 02:05:39,060
...he granted us our every goal.

1014
02:05:40,790 --> 02:05:42,310
Thankfully, my Osman.

1015
02:05:42,770 --> 02:05:44,170
With the will of Allah and...

1016
02:05:44,430 --> 02:05:47,380
...with the strength of you and those
under your command.

1017
02:05:47,440 --> 02:05:50,200
No, don't spare yourself.

1018
02:05:51,410 --> 02:05:53,100
A state lives with the mothers.

1019
02:05:54,490 --> 02:05:56,900
If I didn't have a mother like you
behind me...

1020
02:05:57,650 --> 02:05:59,110
...my family...

1021
02:05:59,910 --> 02:06:01,350
...it'd be nothing like this.

1022
02:06:02,250 --> 02:06:04,410
Your love warms my heart, my Osman.

1023
02:06:05,060 --> 02:06:07,650
There is the fire of our love in my heart.

1024
02:06:08,160 --> 02:06:10,360
I would go anywhere with you, Osman Bey.

1025
02:06:13,290 --> 02:06:14,970
My brave hatun!

1026
02:06:16,060 --> 02:06:18,250
As long as I have my family behind me...

1027
02:06:19,190 --> 02:06:23,310
...nothing can decrease my strength,
thankfully.

1028
02:06:27,360 --> 02:06:31,070
I hope our children will be brave, honest
...

1029
02:06:31,190 --> 02:06:33,740
...and faithful like you.

1030
02:06:35,200 --> 02:06:37,160
What makes a son a Bey is his mother.

1031
02:06:37,940 --> 02:06:40,040
They will be as you raise them.

1032
02:06:40,430 --> 02:06:41,500
But...

1033
02:06:42,010 --> 02:06:46,280
...I hope they will have your patience and
wisdom so that...

1034
02:06:46,520 --> 02:06:50,220
...our state rules the whole world.

1035
02:06:51,540 --> 02:06:52,480
But...

1036
02:06:54,290 --> 02:06:57,600
... who can stand against those who have
a mother like you?

1037
02:07:14,500 --> 02:07:15,490
Praise be!

1038
02:07:15,720 --> 02:07:19,370
Praise be! Osman Bey built his dream
in this tribe.

1039
02:07:20,280 --> 02:07:23,230
Now, he makes conquests after conquests.

1040
02:07:24,470 --> 02:07:25,460
Right.

1041
02:07:25,850 --> 02:07:29,930
Avoiding war doesn't get anything to Beys.

1042
02:07:30,760 --> 02:07:32,150
War will continue so that...

1043
02:07:32,320 --> 02:07:33,790
...the tribe grows.

1044
02:07:34,670 --> 02:07:38,250
Conquest is the lifeblood of Turks.

1045
02:07:38,630 --> 02:07:41,390
He will drink and drink so that the Turks
grow.

1046
02:07:42,150 --> 02:07:44,430
The state Osman Bey will establish will be
...

1047
02:07:44,610 --> 02:07:47,490
...a hope for all Turkmens.

1048
02:07:49,000 --> 02:07:53,590
Supporting his cause is an honor for
Çobanoğlu.

1049
02:07:55,590 --> 02:07:58,710
Since you are this thirsty for conquest...

1050
02:07:59,590 --> 02:08:01,830
...you will stay with Osman Bey.

1051
02:08:02,330 --> 02:08:04,180
You will be under his command.

1052
02:08:05,750 --> 02:08:09,890
Guzzle the lifeblood, son.

1053
02:08:25,810 --> 02:08:26,630
Brother...

1054
02:08:27,030 --> 02:08:29,160
...you fought many wars with my father.

1055
02:08:29,350 --> 02:08:31,990
When do you think I can fight the
infidels?

1056
02:08:34,760 --> 02:08:36,660
I was impatient too.

1057
02:08:37,060 --> 02:08:38,660
But time flies by.

1058
02:08:40,490 --> 02:08:43,620
One day you'll look and see a sword
in your hand.

1059
02:08:44,040 --> 02:08:46,010
I hope so, brother.

1060
02:08:51,860 --> 02:08:53,060
My mother is coming.

1061
02:08:54,580 --> 02:08:55,480
Mother!

1062
02:08:58,680 --> 02:09:01,330
Why are you carrying these while there are
many hatuns?

1063
02:09:02,290 --> 02:09:03,450
You see, Ayşe?

1064
02:09:04,040 --> 02:09:06,090
They grew up and don't let us do
hardwork.

1065
02:09:06,090 --> 02:09:08,090
Praise be! Praise be!

1066
02:09:08,280 --> 02:09:10,920
-Thankfully.
-Thankfully.

1067
02:09:12,210 --> 02:09:14,950
My Ahmed sent news. He is coming back.

1068
02:09:15,110 --> 02:09:18,280
They can't make it today but they
will be here tomorrow, I hope.

1069
02:09:18,850 --> 02:09:20,210
I hope so.

1070
02:09:20,970 --> 02:09:22,210
Come on.

1071
02:09:26,650 --> 02:09:29,010
How is Konya?

1072
02:09:29,560 --> 02:09:32,790
-Is its wind hard?
-It is, my Sheik.

1073
02:09:33,300 --> 02:09:37,350
It is so hard that the seeds of the state
get dispersed around the world by it.

1074
02:09:38,020 --> 02:09:41,480
This is where the Turkish state will
flourish.

1075
02:09:42,820 --> 02:09:47,640
Allah is the one who blows the wind and
makes the seed grow.

1076
02:09:49,890 --> 02:09:54,690
Tell me about my daughter,
my grandchildren, Dursun.

1077
02:09:55,490 --> 02:09:57,330
They pray for your health, my Sheik.

1078
02:09:58,730 --> 02:10:00,420
I've prepared their convoys.

1079
02:10:01,320 --> 02:10:02,600
The reunion is soon.

1080
02:10:03,350 --> 02:10:04,740
They will come.

1081
02:10:06,130 --> 02:10:09,000
Thankfully! Thankfully!

1082
02:10:11,270 --> 02:10:14,500
Did you say goodbye to your students?

1083
02:10:15,640 --> 02:10:17,700
I left the professorship behind me.

1084
02:10:18,710 --> 02:10:19,510
Now...

1085
02:10:20,050 --> 02:10:25,890
...I am a messenger who will convey Sultan
Alaaddin's trust to Osman Bey.

1086
02:10:26,950 --> 02:10:30,100
I am ready for the duty my Bey
assigned me.

1087
02:10:31,430 --> 02:10:34,600
Your duty is already ready, Dursun.

1088
02:11:36,500 --> 02:11:40,850
We need skills in pen as much as we do
in sword.

1089
02:11:42,410 --> 02:11:44,870
Obviously, your coming is blessed.

1090
02:11:47,450 --> 02:11:51,250
The signs he brings are the signs of
the state to be established.

1091
02:11:52,050 --> 02:11:53,410
The pen is here.

1092
02:11:57,480 --> 02:12:00,010
The state is near, right brother?

1093
02:12:02,420 --> 02:12:03,620
Brothers...

1094
02:12:04,630 --> 02:12:07,850
...you keep what you took by sword with
knowledge.

1095
02:12:08,490 --> 02:12:09,570
You are right.

1096
02:12:11,450 --> 02:12:13,690
Come on, let's go to Osman Bey.

1097
02:12:40,450 --> 02:12:41,620
From now on...

1098
02:12:42,850 --> 02:12:47,510
...just like Bilecik, İnegöl...

1099
02:12:48,310 --> 02:12:50,200
...and the whole Hisar...

1100
02:12:50,790 --> 02:12:52,620
...Yeni Şehir is the property of Kayı.

1101
02:13:00,440 --> 02:13:05,650
We know that our people are bigger
than Kayı.

1102
02:13:07,410 --> 02:13:11,810
And we will make a move according to
the greatness.

1103
02:13:12,920 --> 02:13:16,040
In these lands where the flag of Islam
flies...

1104
02:13:17,140 --> 02:13:21,080
...there will be no cruelty or injustice!

1105
02:13:41,080 --> 02:13:42,360
Welcome.

1106
02:13:43,510 --> 02:13:45,220
Thank you, Osman Bey.

1107
02:13:48,070 --> 02:13:52,340
These are Sultan Alaaddin's signs to Osman
Bey.

1108
02:13:54,440 --> 02:13:59,090
He sent you a fast and robust horse.

1109
02:14:05,770 --> 02:14:07,890
He tells you not to stop the conquests.

1110
02:14:17,270 --> 02:14:19,670
In the name of Allah.

1111
02:14:22,710 --> 02:14:27,010
He sent Quran which was written by skilled
calligraphers.

1112
02:14:28,100 --> 02:14:31,590
He tells you to always order by Quran.

1113
02:14:38,690 --> 02:14:41,450
In the name of Allah.

1114
02:14:59,670 --> 02:15:01,850
He sent you the sharpest sword.

1115
02:15:03,140 --> 02:15:05,570
So that the oppressors can't stand against
you.

1116
02:15:30,010 --> 02:15:34,500
Sultan congratulates your conquest,
Osman Bey.

1117
02:15:34,760 --> 02:15:35,750
Thank him.

1118
02:15:37,080 --> 02:15:39,030
And thank you, Dursun Faki.

1119
02:15:39,940 --> 02:15:44,250
Conquests are for the sake of Turks
and Islam.

1120
02:16:13,370 --> 02:16:15,560
Sultan is opening our way for us.

1121
02:16:17,780 --> 02:16:22,810
We will walk it as long as we are alive.

1122
02:16:25,570 --> 02:16:29,880
We won't stop until the world feels small
to us.

1123
02:16:32,549 --> 02:16:36,870
Islam is the religion of justice.

1124
02:16:37,940 --> 02:16:43,370
And we will spread this religion to
the whole world!

1125
02:16:45,879 --> 02:16:49,480
Wherever there is cruelty and injustice...

1126
02:16:50,308 --> 02:16:55,990
...we will hit it with the sword of
justice!

1127
02:17:00,280 --> 02:17:01,888
Now our goal is...

1128
02:17:03,320 --> 02:17:05,000
...Bursa on one hand...

1129
02:17:06,770 --> 02:17:08,870
...and İznik on the other hand!

1130
02:17:11,240 --> 02:17:13,160
Yeni Şehir will be our capital.

1131
02:17:15,490 --> 02:17:16,808
From now on...

1132
02:17:17,930 --> 02:17:20,820
...it will be our headquarter for
the conquests!

1133
02:17:24,500 --> 02:17:25,379
My Beys!

1134
02:17:27,010 --> 02:17:27,888
My brothers!

1135
02:17:29,330 --> 02:17:31,058
We get our power...

1136
02:17:33,218 --> 02:17:35,430
...from our cause!

1137
02:17:36,690 --> 02:17:40,629
But we get our strength from those...

1138
02:17:41,959 --> 02:17:43,888
...who always support us...

1139
02:17:44,930 --> 02:17:50,250
...and are no different from the men
of Kayı, our Hatuns!

1140
02:17:53,480 --> 02:17:55,459
From our Alps!

1141
02:17:56,850 --> 02:18:01,320
From our valiants whose hearts are made of
steel!

1142
02:18:02,308 --> 02:18:07,610
From our beys who fill their flags with
winds!

1143
02:18:13,138 --> 02:18:15,808
As long as the Turks have you...

1144
02:18:17,730 --> 02:18:20,180
...no one can stop us!

1145
02:18:21,968 --> 02:18:24,308
Until the sky goes down...

1146
02:18:25,250 --> 02:18:27,650
...and the earth breaks down...

1147
02:18:28,888 --> 02:18:34,170
...who can stop you?

1148
02:18:39,290 --> 02:18:45,160
Not spreading our cause to the whole world
...

1149
02:18:46,440 --> 02:18:47,990
...is haram to us!

1150
02:18:52,410 --> 02:18:53,530
Allah is the greatest!

1151
02:18:53,968 --> 02:19:21,138
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1152
02:19:21,218 --> 02:19:29,070
End of season 3
See you on the next season!

1153
02:19:29,315 --> 02:19:39,275
